{"type":"text","timestamp":1794230075203,"sessionID":"ses_e3f8efd53ffePcqwajAMP1G0aH","part":{"id":"prt_1c071fbd50011L4CfJiV8swAQg","sessionID":"ses_e3f8efd53ffePcqwajAMP1G0aH","messageID":"msg_1c0716d5b001BWLU7KiCoFGqpc","type":"text","text":"Here's a structured example of using the `opencode.models` tool to search for available chat models, along with a practical use case:\n\n```javascript\n// Example: Search for available chat models from OpenAI provider\nawait tools.opencode.models({\n  provider: \"openai\",  // Filter by provider\n  type: \"chat\",        // Specify model type\n  limit: 10,           // Limit results to 10\n  all: false           // Only show the latest version\n});\n\n// Output might look like:\n{\n  providers: [\n    {\n      id: \"openai\",\n      name: \"OpenAI\",\n      models: [\n        {\n          id: \"openai/gpt-4\",\n          name: \"GPT-4\",\n          released: 1680000000000,\n          variants: [\"chat\", \"completion\"],\n          cost: [...],\n          status: \"active\"\n        },\n        // ... other models\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  total: 15,\n  next: 10  // Offset for next page\n}\n```\n\n**Use Case:**  \nWhen a user asks, *\"Show me the latest OpenAI chat models available for use\"*, this call retrieves the relevant models, allowing you to present their details, pricing, and capabilities.\n\n---\n\n### Key Tool Usage Patterns\n\n1. **`opencode.models`**  \n   - **When to use:** Convert vague model names into precise references.  \n   - **Example:**  \n     ```javascript\n     await tools.opencode.models({ query: \"gpt-3.5\", type: \"chat\" });\n     ```\n\n2. **`roslyn.get_public_api_surface`**  \n   - **When to use:** Analyze public APIs in a solution.  \n   - **Example:**  \n     ```javascript\n     await tools.roslyn.get_public_api_surface();\n     ```\n\n3. **`opencode.list_mcp_resources`**  \n   - **When to use:** Access external data from MCP servers.  \n   - **Example:**  \n     ```javascript\n     await tools.opencode.list_mcp_resources({ server: \"exampleServer\" });\n     ```\n\n4. **`roslyn.get_project_dependencies`**  \n   - **When to use:** Investigate transitive dependencies in a project.  \n   - **Example:**  \n     ```javascript\n     await tools.roslyn.get_project_dependencies({ project: \"MyProject.csproj\" });\n     ```\n\n---\n\n### Best Practices\n- Always specify `type` (e.g., `\"chat\"`, `\"image\"`) when searching models.\n- Use `limit` and `offset` for pagination.\n- For MCP resources, ensure `server` and `uri` are correctly resolved before calling `read_mcp_resource`.\n- Handle errors for tools like `worktree_remove` by checking the `force` flag before execution.","time":{"start":1794230057941,"end":1794230075203}}}
